# Google Integrations

Full detail: `docs/integrations/GOOGLE-INTEGRATIONS.md`.

## Principles

- Least privilege; no whole-Drive access for service accounts.
- Prefer Shared Drive; separate test vs production sources.
- Secrets only in Secret Manager — never in the repo.
- External content is never auto-published.
- No two-way sync without an explicit approved decision (ADR).

## Role of Google

Import and preparation only. Portal DB remains source of truth for published content.

Pipeline: detect → load → normalize → preview version → diff → admin confirm → version → publish → reindex → audit.

## Docs import

Support: headings, paragraphs, bullets, numbered lists, links, tables, images, basic formatting.

Unsupported elements: record as warnings, do not silently drop, show in import report.

## Sheets import

Use for bulk prompts, registries, categories, tags, metadata, learning paths.

Before import: validate column schema → validate all rows → show per-row errors → do not partially import corrupted data without explicit admin permission.

## Drive

Source file selection, collaboration, source images/video/docs. Published media may be copied to Cloud Storage when needed.
